WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.474
Good evening.

2
00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:15.207
Good evening.

3
00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:19.335
Who are you?

4
00:00:19.336 --> 00:00:23.476
I'm a red fox.

5
00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:27.947
Red foxes are mammals.

6
00:00:27.948 --> 00:00:31.720
We look like dogs.

7
00:00:31.721 --> 00:00:34.540
Where do you live?

8
00:00:34.541 --> 00:00:39.971
Red foxes live all over the world.

9
00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:43.172
We like forests.

10
00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:49.691
But we also live in cities and deserts.

11
00:00:49.692 --> 00:00:53.070
You eat mice, right?

12
00:00:53.071 --> 00:00:58.516
Yes. We eat other small animals too.

13
00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:03.323
We like birds and rabbits.

14
00:01:03.324 --> 00:01:09.235
Sometimes we eat fruit—and garbage.

15
00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:12.497
Your ears are big!

16
00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:16.562
Red foxes are good hunters.

17
00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:21.436
Our big ears help us hear prey.

18
00:01:21.437 --> 00:01:24.824
Who are your enemies?

19
00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:28.839
Coyotes and bears hunt us.

20
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.837
People are our enemies too.

21
00:01:32.838 --> 00:01:37.359
They hunt us and build near our dens.

22
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.076
Oh! Is that your den?

23
00:01:41.077 --> 00:01:45.772
Yes. We use dens for sleeping.

24
00:01:45.773 --> 00:01:51.073
Mother foxes keep their babies in dens.

25
00:01:51.074 --> 00:01:54.366
I like your bushy tail!

26
00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:58.518
We use our tails to cover our bodies.

27
00:01:58.519 --> 00:02:07.606
This keeps us warm at nap time.

28
00:02:07.607 --> 00:02:11.181
Shh. I hear a mouse.

29
00:02:11.182 --> 00:02:15.081
I'm going to hunt!

30
00:02:15.082 --> 00:02:20.289
So long, Red Fox!
